build/
cmake-build-*/
compile_commands.json
.ccls-cache/
.ccls-root
src/a3-motion-engine/Config.hh
src/a3-motion-ui/Config.hh
microsoft.gpg
config/ui_state.json

# What the performer brings, not what the repo ships. The recordings are
# somebody's takes and set.json is their arrangement -- live pot positions
# included, so it would churn on every single commit. The system patterns in
# pattern/system/ stay tracked: those are the instrument.
pattern/user/
pattern/set.json
pattern/current.json
pattern/sessions/*
# Ten factory sets -- one per place in an evening, each naming eight shapes
# and carrying a preset per slot. The performer's own sets land in the same
# folder, and current.json is the one actually in use, so these are named
# one by one the way the factory clips are.
!pattern/sessions/Opening.json
!pattern/sessions/Ascent.json
!pattern/sessions/Peak.json
!pattern/sessions/Breakdown.json
!pattern/sessions/Drop.json
!pattern/sessions/Rollers.json
!pattern/sessions/Dub.json
!pattern/sessions/Techno.json
!pattern/sessions/Ambient.json
!pattern/sessions/Dice.json
# The clips that reach the performer's own takes. The factory clips beside them
# are the instrument and stay tracked; these are somebody's evening on it, like
# the takes themselves. They share a folder only until the folders are split
# into a fixed factory tree and a movable user one -- see
# .claude/notes/2026-09-04-clip-und-session-dateien.md, step 4 -- after which
# this pattern-match can go.
# The presets a performer generates and keeps. Default.json is the instrument's
# and is tracked; the rest come out of a3-clip-gen and are somebody's taste.
pattern/clips/*.json
# The factory bank: twenty presets picked by hand, in four groups of five --
# where a clip sits, how fast it turns, how it breathes, how it runs. Named
# one by one rather than matched, because the folder they live in is also
# where a3-clip-gen throws its dice and where the performer keeps their own.
!pattern/clips/Default.json
!pattern/clips/Halo.json
!pattern/clips/Equator.json
!pattern/clips/Cellar.json
!pattern/clips/Dome.json
!pattern/clips/Pinpoint.json
!pattern/clips/Slow Turn.json
!pattern/clips/Carousel.json
!pattern/clips/Whirlwind.json
!pattern/clips/Counter.json
!pattern/clips/Standstill.json
!pattern/clips/Breath.json
!pattern/clips/Tide.json
!pattern/clips/Flutter.json
!pattern/clips/Ebb.json
!pattern/clips/Surge.json
!pattern/clips/Half Time.json
!pattern/clips/Double Time.json
!pattern/clips/Seesaw.json
!pattern/clips/Backspin.json
!pattern/clips/Dice.json

# IDE
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# The performer's own work, not the project's. Recordings, clips, actions and
# sets made on a device belong to that device: a tracked one would be laid
# down on every other checkout, and a deletion on one machine would show up as
# a change to be committed. The instrument's own live in the system/ halves
# beside these and are tracked.
pattern/user/
pattern/clips/user/
pattern/actions/user/
pattern/sessions/user/
